Publish-ready Substack version of the research blog, plus PNG exports of all figures.

## Contents
- **`docs/publication/research_blog_substack.md`** — the Substack-ready post. Critical-editor pass over the existing draft:
  - corrected the "78%" framing (it's 78% of the *advantage over baseline*, not of recall);
  - explained the +0.094 residual that survives fully-scrambled importance (tie-breaking perturbation, not signal — zeroing the importance term collapses to baseline);
  - added two omitted caveats (the −0.32 correlation is over only 6 tasks → descriptive, not significant; the behavioral contrast depends on a tight retrieval budget);
  - defined metrics on first use (recall@5, MRR, paired bootstrap) for a broader audience;
  - figures embedded as `![caption](file.png)` markers.
- **`docs/papers/figures/*.png`** — 2× PNG exports of all ten figures (data figures 3–9 via headless Chrome; TikZ diagrams 1/2/10 via ghostscript).
- **`docs/papers/figures/export_png.py`** — reproducible SVG→PNG driver.

No research artifacts, claims, numbers, or the benchmark were modified. Independent of PR #29 (release hygiene).

